<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Penne, Abruzzo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pinna Vestinorum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Penne is a hill town in the province of Pescara, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abruzzo">Abruzzo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gran-sasso">Gran Sasso</a> and the Adriatic. As Pinna it was the chief town of the Vestini, which sided with the Italian allies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-war-91-87-bce">Social War</a> of 91–88 BCE, and later a Roman municipium. It was a bishopric from early times, and its brick-built old town is one of the best preserved in Abruzzo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/penne-abruzzo.jpg" alt="Penne, Abruzzo" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LigaDue · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PenneAbruzzoPanorama1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
